{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1110776-bugs-and-snakes-and-bats-oh-my","id":1110776,"title":"Bugs and snakes and bats...oh my","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-03T00:25:42-07:00","id":1110776,"title":"Bugs and snakes and bats...oh my","content":"So got myself Dankest Dungeon DLC called Crimson Court. It is obviously about vamps but with insect motive(giant tick for head brrrry). So I have two quesions<br /> <br /> 1. What insect related powers and themes do we have in requiem. I know of swarm form and flood of vermin and also adopted infestation from Beast as expansion of swarm form. I think there was beethemed bloodline(melisomething) but not sure if that was from purely metaphorical standpoint or were there real bees involved. <br /> <br /> 2. What other out of whack vampires did you encounter in fiction?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12924-orzhov","name":"Orzhov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-03T00:41:41-07:00","id":1110779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Orzhov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1110776-bugs-and-snakes-and-bats-oh-my#post1110776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. What insect related powers and themes do we have in requiem. I know of swarm form and flood of vermin and also adopted infestation from Beast as expansion of swarm form. I think there was beethemed bloodline(melisomething) but not sure if that was from purely metaphorical standpoint or were there real bees involved.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's the obvious ones, Animalism and Protean. We had a thread about it <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/536189-gangrel-insects\">here</a>. The Bloodline is the Melissidae, and it is not entirely metaphorical, the bees are only technically involved with the origin but the themes weave in and out. While their Vitae tastes like honey, the vampire is Queen Bee, and her bonded her drones. It's in Bloodlines the Legendary, great bloodline.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. What other out of whack vampires did you encounter in fiction? </div> </div> </div>Charlee Jacob does some interesting things with their relationship with the sun, but in a Symbiotic Fascination, Tawny the vampire was swarmed by moths whenever dawn approached. Richard Laymon goes the other way, playing up their human disguise and reveling in how humanlike they can be, or how monstrous humans can be. There's several vampires in his books and it's never clear if they're actually vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-03T00:55:34-07:00","id":1110783,"title":"","content":"This reminds me. There are &quot;Vampires&quot; in Peter Watts sf Blindsight. But they are just super smart cannibals that due to brain defect suffer seizures at the sight of straight lines and need to take medicine to alleviate that. Could work as an idea for Slasher imho","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12924-orzhov","name":"Orzhov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}